  "line": 1324,
  "title": "The push guard still runs before the retried push, not at it",
  "detail": "pushExistingBranch calls guard() once and then hands the push to remoteSh, which goes through withGitHubRetry (src/git/repos.ts ~115): after a transient failure it pauses for seconds and runs the push again without consulting the guard, and cacheGit also awaits before it spawns (src/git/command.ts ~140). A reclaim during that pause still lets the stale worker push. Call the guard inside the retried operation, synchronously immediately before each push attempt spawns (the merge path already does this on every retry), so a lost claim stops every attempt. Add a test where the first push fails transiently, the entry is reclaimed during the retry delay, and no second push runs. The existing test at test/land-queue.test.ts ~2923 reclaims inside the guard itself, so it doesn't cover this."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 843,
  "title": "Per-attempt checkouts leak the base export after a crash",
  "detail": "Checks export the base commit to `${cwd}-base`, i.e. land-<id>-<attempt>-base. Before this change every attempt reused land-<id>-base, so the next attempt's rmSync removed a crashed attempt's export; now each attempt has a new path, and the stale-checkout sweep in checkout() only matches a numeric attempt suffix, so land-<id>-<n>-base (and a legacy land-<id>-base) are never removed after a daemon restart during checks. Remove abandoned base exports for earlier attempts (and the legacy name) in the same sweep, as plain directories, not worktrees. Add a test that leaves a stale base export from an earlier attempt and asserts the next attempt removes it."
 }
]
